examples.jsonl contains code excerpts from the godot-rust project (https://github.com/godot-rust):
the book, demo-projects and gdext's integration tests. They are licensed under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). Each entry's "src" field names the file it came from.
Entries whose "src" starts with "godot-demo-projects" come from the Godot demo projects
(https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects), MIT License, Copyright (c) Juan Linietsky,
Ariel Manzur and contributors. Rebuild with training/build_examples.py.

Entries whose "src" starts with "github" come from open-source projects found by
training/crawl_github.py. Only permissively licensed repos are used, and the license is named in
each entry's "src". Entries marked "ember-verified" are RusticEngine's own training examples.

Blender Manual excerpts (design.jsonl entries with "kind": "manual")
  The Blender Manual by the Blender Documentation Team (https://projects.blender.org/blender/documentation),
  https://docs.blender.org/manual/, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  Text was converted from reStructuredText and shortened; each entry links its source page.

Wikipedia excerpts (design.jsonl entries with "kind": "game")
  Short excerpts of Wikipedia articles about games, from Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia
  (https://en.wikipedia.org), licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  Each entry's "url" links its article, whose history lists the authors. Text was shortened.

Design patterns (design.jsonl entries with "kind": "pattern")
  The code in these entries is RusticEngine's own godot-rust code (GPL-3.0), written to show a design
  idea. The "source" field credits the game whose design inspired it; no code from those games is included.

Blender library (blender.jsonl, blender_keys.json; built by training/build_blender_kb.py)
  - "kind": "manual": the Blender Manual by the Blender Documentation Team, https://docs.blender.org/manual/,
    CC BY-SA 4.0. Converted from reStructuredText and split by section; each entry links its page.
  - "kind": "concept": excerpts of Wikipedia articles (https://en.wikipedia.org), CC BY-SA 4.0. Each entry's
    "url" links its article, whose history lists the authors. Text was split by section and shortened.
  - "kind": "keymap" and blender_keys.json: Blender 5.2's default keymap, read from Blender (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  - "kind": "resource": names and links from the Poly Haven (https://polyhaven.com) and ambientCG
    (https://ambientcg.com) catalogues; the assets themselves are CC0 and are not included.
  - "kind": "extension": names, taglines and licenses from the Blender Extensions platform
    (https://extensions.blender.org); the extensions are not included.
  - "kind": "guide": RusticEngine's own Blender Art Paths (agent/paths/art-blender-*.md, GPL-3.0).
